      "content": "While your experience is fascinating, the belief that HFT algorithms respond to human cognitive patterns is highly speculative. High-frequency trading relies on incredibly fast, deterministic computational processes operating on market data. The perceived synchronization is more likely a product of confirmation bias interacting with the visually complex and rapid data stream. Current technology does not support the idea of direct neural-to-algorithmic communication through market latency.",
